{"id":"638ef03c09b1","html":"<p><img src=\"https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224604/default-7.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"662\" height=\"1000\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 662px) 100vw, 662px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Over 100,000 people move to the San Francisco Bay Area each year. Their motivations for doing so no doubt vary, but these days, the ambition to make a fortune at the epicenter of the tech industry — especially amid the rapidly inflating AI bubble — is hardly unheard of. Unfortunately, that desire can be so all-consuming as to crowd out any interest in, or even curiosity about, the city itself, to say nothing of its wider region. Yet the San Francisco we know today is the result of a story at least 250 years long, very little of which has much to do with venture capital or GPUs. Now, anyone who does want to make a start on understanding it can do so at the new-and-improved platform <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DigitalSF</a>, with its more than 80,000 historical items <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">available to view and download</a>.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224603/default-6.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1000\" height=\"801\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>An operation of the San Francisco Public Library, <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DigitalSF</a> offers simultaneous access to multiple online historical archives. Search for the <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Golden%20Gate%20Bridge&amp;f=&amp;c=Archives%20of%20the%20City%20and%20County%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Digitized%20Book%20Collection&amp;c=Hormel%20LGBTQIA%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20Historical%20Photograph%20Collection&amp;c=Shades%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Book%20Arts%20%26%20Special%20Collections%20Center&amp;c=Government%20Information%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=Branch%20Archives%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20History%20Center%20Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Golden Gate Bridge</a>, let’s say, and the results will include hundreds of postcard photographs and other images capturing that iconic piece of infrastructure from a variety of angles and in a variety of decades, as well as&nbsp;— since this is the always climatically surprising San Francisco we’re talking about — under a variety of weather conditions.</p>\n\n\n<p>The same exercise would prove equally illuminating for <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Chinatown&amp;f=&amp;c=Archives%20of%20the%20City%20and%20County%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Digitized%20Book%20Collection&amp;c=Hormel%20LGBTQIA%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20Historical%20Photograph%20Collection&amp;c=Shades%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Book%20Arts%20%26%20Special%20Collections%20Center&amp;c=Government%20Information%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=Branch%20Archives%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20History%20Center%20Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chinatown</a>, <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=pier%2039&amp;f=&amp;c=Archives%20of%20the%20City%20and%20County%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Digitized%20Book%20Collection&amp;c=Hormel%20LGBTQIA%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20Historical%20Photograph%20Collection&amp;c=Shades%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Book%20Arts%20%26%20Special%20Collections%20Center&amp;c=Government%20Information%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=Branch%20Archives%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20History%20Center%20Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pier 39</a>, the <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Sutro+Baths&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sutro Baths</a> (which weren’t always ruins), and&nbsp;the <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Ferry+Building&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ferry Building</a> (which wasn’t always a collection of pricey shops). Inevitably, this sort of virtual tourism becomes a form of time travel.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02224541/OC-San-Francisco-postcard.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1000\" height=\"641\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DigitalSF</a> also offers countless glimpses of San Francisco’s important periods in twentieth-century American counterculture, when the city made everything seem possible: <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=beatniks&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">beatnik poetry</a>, the <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Grateful+Dead&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Grateful Dead</a>, a particular flavor of <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=punk&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">punk</a>, the ascent of <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=Harvey%20Milk&amp;f=&amp;c=Archives%20of%20the%20City%20and%20County%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Digitized%20Book%20Collection&amp;c=Hormel%20LGBTQIA%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20Historical%20Photograph%20Collection&amp;c=Shades%20of%20San%20Francisco&amp;c=Book%20Arts%20%26%20Special%20Collections%20Center&amp;c=Government%20Information%20Center%20Collection&amp;c=Branch%20Archives%20Collection&amp;c=San%20Francisco%20History%20Center%20Collection&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Harvey Milk</a>. But even before then, San Francisco had already experienced a disproportionately intense amount of history during its relatively short existence: the earthquakes of <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=1868+earthquake&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1868</a> and <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=1906+earthquake&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1906</a>, for example,&nbsp;or the <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=%22gold+rush%22&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gold Rush</a> of the late eighteen-forties from whose participants the <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/search?ln=en&amp;p=49ers&amp;f=&amp;action_search=Search&amp;rm=&amp;sf=&amp;so=d&amp;rg=25&amp;c=Archives+of+the+City+and+County+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=Book+Arts+%26+Special+Collections+Center&amp;c=Branch+Archives+Collection&amp;c=Digitized+Book+Collection&amp;c=Government+Information+Center+Collection&amp;c=Hormel+LGBTQIA+Center+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+Historical+Photograph+Collection&amp;c=San+Francisco+History+Center+Collection&amp;c=Shades+of+San+Francisco&amp;c=&amp;fti=1&amp;fti=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">local football team</a> took its name. Those “forty-niners” who flooded in from all over the rest of the United States, turning San Francisco from a small port town into a relatively major city practically overnight, probably had scant fascination with local history themselves. After all, they were too busy making it. Enter the <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DigitalSF</a> <a href=\"https://digitalsf.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cdn8.openculture.com/2026/11/02225936/default-8.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1000\" height=\"666\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p><strong>Related content:</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.openculture.com/2014/06/5000-images-from-the-san-francisco-municipal-transportation-agency-photographic-archive.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">An Archive of 5,000 Images Document the History of San Francisco and the Vehicles That Put It in Motion</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.openculture.com/2018/05/see-footage-of-san-francisco-right-before-after-the-massively-devastating-earthquake-of-1906.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dramatic Footage of San Francisco Right Before &amp; After the Massively Devastating Earthquake of 1906</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.openculture.com/2026/02/how-the-golden-gate-bridge-was-built-a-3d-animated-introduction.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How the Golden Gate Bridge Was Built: A 3D Animated Introduction</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.openculture.com/2014/09/rare-footage-of-human-be-in.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rare Footage of the “Human Be-In,” the Landmark Counter-Culture Event Held in Golden Gate Park, 1967</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.openculture.com/2010/09/the_unseen_sea_san_francisco_beauty_in_hd.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Unseen Sea: San Francisco Natural Beauty in HD</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.openculture.com/2019/03/lawrence-ferlinghetti-turns-100-hear-the-great-san-francisco-poet-read-trumps-trojan-horse-pity-the-nation-many-other-poems.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lawrence Ferlinghetti Turns 100: Hear the Great San Francisco Poet Read “Trump’s Trojan Horse,” “Pity the Nation” &amp; Many Other Poems</a></p>\n<p><em>Based in Seoul, </em><em><a href=\"http://blog.colinmarshall.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Colin</a></em><em><a href=\"http://blog.colinmarshall.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">&nbsp;M</a></em><em><a href=\"http://blog.colinmarshall.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">a</a></em><em><a href=\"http://blog.colinmarshall.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">rshall</a>&nbsp;writes and broadcas</em><em>ts on cities, language, and culture. He’s the author of the newsletter</em>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://colinmarshall.substack.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Books on Cities</a><em>&nbsp;as well as the books&nbsp;</em><a href=\"https://product.kyobobook.co.kr/detail/S000212263515\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">한국 요약 금지</a><em>&nbsp;(No Summarizing Korea) and&nbsp;</em><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Korean-Newtro-Where-Youth-Tradition/dp/156591533X\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Korean Newtro</a><em>.</em>&nbsp;<em>Follow him on the social network formerly known as Twitter at&nbsp;<a href=\"https://twitter.com/#%21/colinmarshall\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">@colinm</a></em><em><a href=\"https://twitter.com/#%21/colinmarshall\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">a</a></em><em><a href=\"https://twitter.com/#%21/colinmarshall\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">rshall</a>.</em></p>"}